  "summary": "In July 1908 army officers backing the Committee of Union and Progress rose in Macedonia, led at first by Major Ahmed Niyazi. On 24 July Sultan Abdulhamid II, in Constantinople, restored the 1876 constitution and agreed to elections. The revolution opened the Second Constitutional Period of the Ottoman Empire.",
